 "reporting": "Percent resistant by pathogen and specimen (blood, pus aspirate, other sterile body fluids, urine; Salmonella and Shigella tables not split by specimen), all location types pooled, with number tested and number resistant; blood isolates also charted by location type (OPD, IPD, ICU) with printed data labels; MRSA and VRE yearly trend charts.",
 "method": "WHONET collation and analysis; CLSI interpretive criteria; disc diffusion, broth microdilution and automated AST at the sites; colistin by broth microdilution per CLSI M02 and M100 (limited number of isolates); first isolate per patient, specimen type and pathogen (45,397 isolates reported, 40,323 unique-patient isolates). Percentages not computed when fewer than 30 isolates were tested.",
 "breakpoints": "CLSI, edition not stated",
