 "verification": {
  "status": "double-checked",
  "note": "Tables 4 to 11 parsed from the PDF text layer (pdfplumber words assigned to columns by x position) and every value compared by eye with the pages rendered at scale 2.2; every printed percentage recomputed from its printed counts (three disagreements, all in the Table 7 blood column, recorded as conflicts). Figures 7 to 12 (blood by location): data labels from the text layer, each matched to its bar by a script comparing the bar colour on the page rendered at scale 4 with the legend (OPD grey, IPD orange, ICU blue), labels without a bar (0%) placed by their position in the group, then every label checked by eye on the rendered chart; the text statement for Pseudomonas ceftazidime (ICU 46%, IPD 30%, OPD 17%) confirms the order. MRSA and VRE trend labels read from the rendered charts (one bar per year in legend order). Count Tables 2 and 3 checked against the images and their printed totals. Page numbers are 1-based PDF pages."
 },
 "notes": "Kerala state antibiogram (KARS-Net Annual Report 2024), data from 1 January to 31 December 2023: 34 laboratories in 11 districts (49 network sites at publication). All figures are percent resistant (intermediate counted as not resistant). Specimen PA (pus aspirate) is shown under deep infections (aspirates) and OSBF (other sterile body fluids) as sterile. The specimen tables pool all location types (set all); blood rows by location (OPD, IPD, ICU) come from the bar charts. The Salmonella table covers blood and stool isolates together (recorded as all specimens). The all-specimen S. aureus (cefoxitin) and Enterococcus (vancomycin) rows carry the MRSA and VRE yearly trends. Drugs printed \"-\" (fewer than 30 tested) are left out. In Table 7 the blood ceftriaxone, cefotaxime and cefepime counts do not give the printed percentages (recorded as conflicts; the location chart, Figure 10, is in line with the printed percentages).",
 "issues": [
  "Second reader 2026-09-26: every cell re-read blind against the page images before comparing (all 479 cells, including the seeded sample of 120, plus all 45 row n and all 50 counts; tables at scale 2.5, charts zoomed at scale 4): 0 transcription errors, nothing corrected.",
  "Second reader: all 204 location-chart cells (Figures 7 to 12) also checked by a script that samples each figure's own legend marker colours (OPD grey, IPD orange, ICU blue in every 2023 figure) and the colour of the bar behind each data label (25 zero labels without a bar placed by their slot): drug, location and value agree for every cell.",
  "Second reader: the three caution cells are printed that way (re-read at scale 5): Table 7 blood Klebsiella prints ceftriaxone 366 tested, 197 resistant, 69%; cefotaxime 741, 143, 74% (the page 35 text also says 74%); cefepime 853, 480, 64%. The Figure 10 location values weighted by their legend N give 68%, 72% and 64%, in line with the printed percentages; conflicts kept.",
  "Second reader: every printed percentage of Tables 4 to 11 recomputed from its printed counts; no other disagreement.",
  "Second reader: added as counts (all specimens, all settings) the isolate totals per organism printed in Figure 2, page 22 (after de-duplication; they sum to 40,323 and equal the Table 2 and Table 3 sums).",
  "Lead 2026-09-26: \"pus aspirate\" (NCDC SOP category) filed under specimen \"deep\" (deep infections, aspirates), as for the other NCDC-protocol networks; 6 rows and 6 counts moved from \"pus\"."
 ],
